q=b8?"Know what FreeFOP is and when to try it.":"Bi\u1ebft FreeFOP l\xe0 g\xec v\xe0 khi n\xe0o n\xean th\u1eed."
p=b8?'FreeFOP = "Free" + F2L + OLL + PLL: instead of a cross then pairs, freely build a 2\xd72\xd72 or 2\xd72\xd73 block, then finish the rest of F2L.':'FreeFOP = "Free" + F2L + OLL + PLL: thay v\xec l\xe0m d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng r\u1ed3i t\u1eebng c\u1eb7p, d\u1ef1ng t\u1ef1 do m\u1ed9t kh\u1ed1i 2\xd72\xd72 ho\u1eb7c 2\xd72\xd73, sau \u0111\xf3 ho\xe0n th\xe0nh ph\u1ea7n F2L c\xf2n l\u1ea1i.'
o=b8?"Pros: fewer moves when the cube has a block ready; the last layer is still the OLL/PLL you know.":"\u01afu \u0111i\u1ec3m: \xedt b\u01b0\u1edbc h\u01a1n khi cube c\xf3 s\u1eb5n kh\u1ed1i; t\u1ea7ng cu\u1ed1i v\u1eabn l\xe0 OLL/PLL quen thu\u1ed9c n\xean kh\xf4ng ph\u1ea3i h\u1ecdc l\u1ea1i."
n=b8?'Cons: harder look-ahead than CFOP, needs strong inspection. Most fast solvers stay with CFOP and "borrow" the block idea on easy scrambles.':'Nh\u01b0\u1ee3c \u0111i\u1ec3m: kh\xf3 nh\xecn tr\u01b0\u1edbc h\u01a1n CFOP, c\u1ea7n quan s\xe1t gi\u1ecfi. Ph\u1ea7n l\u1edbn ng\u01b0\u1eddi gi\u1ea3i nhanh v\u1eabn d\xf9ng CFOP v\xe0 ch\u1ec9 "m\u01b0\u1ee3n" \xfd t\u01b0\u1edfng kh\u1ed1i khi g\u1eb7p x\xe1o d\u1ec5.'
m=b8?"A 2\xd72\xd72 block: one white corner + its 3 edges + 3 centres. Look around for a corner that already has 1\u20132 edges attached.":"Kh\u1ed1i 2\xd72\xd72: m\u1ed9t g\xf3c tr\u1eafng + 3 c\u1ea1nh quanh n\xf3 + 3 t\xe2m. Nh\xecn quanh cube xem g\xf3c n\xe0o \u0111\xe3 c\xf3 s\u1eb5n 1\u20132 c\u1ea1nh d\xednh v\xe0o."
p=A.a([p,o,n,m,b8?"Want to really build blocks? Try Roux (Learn \u2192 Roux & ZZ) \u2013 the whole method is block-building.":"Mu\u1ed1n d\u1ef1ng kh\u1ed1i th\u1eadt s\u1ef1? Xem Roux (H\u1ecdc \u2192 Roux & ZZ) \u2013 c\u1ea3 ph\u01b0\u01a1ng ph\xe1p l\xe0 d\u1ef1ng kh\u1ed1i."],s)
